d "q-43817" :question/id #uuid "03a66baa-aa45-5430-913b-f79634c2af38" :question/math-academy-id "q-43817" :question/problem "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1+i \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2-i\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1+i \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =(-1+i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{1+i})+1\\cdot \\overset{―}{3}+(2-i)\\cdot \\overset{―}{1} \\\\  & =(-1+i)\\cdot (1-i)+1\\cdot 3+(2-i)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\text{i}+3+(2-i) \\\\  & =5+i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43817/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85ae774f-2496-56c0-a800-450bd8383092"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43817"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e4622167-cb75-5159-a99f-28399d0d21cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2c1a0728-b6ce-5cc5-8627-6825e57c538a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "16ce4e59-5862-5e14-836a-f4d84baebc40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "ec818b58-543a-5d33-8c6e-65bfcc04a757" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f4aa4667-1865-5528-933f-5bc88576414f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16991709-53aa-52e3-b461-bee5e6b8d6bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97303/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-97303/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-97303/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-97303/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-97303/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-97303/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97303" :question/id #uuid "ceaeef65-5cc5-5bd2-865b-0a244110fe3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97303" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨b,a⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨-ia,b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. A complex  inner product is linear  in the first argument,  so we have \n\n$$\n⟨-ia,b⟩=-i⟨a,b⟩\\ne i⟨a,b⟩,\n$$\n\nin general.\n\n- Statement III is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97303/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97303"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "ae80f021-02b8-513c-87f2-99fa175a06c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "181d6878-54c8-523b-9328-0b0a31098a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0c9e4dc7-12a7-5d5c-81c5-b582ddd29819" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "524ac6b3-2e16-535b-86bb-1a3a744dd3ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "617a3510-3ce9-54a9-b908-273b7d5e09b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5685e55-d64b-5b7b-8a58-02ad62c79e1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141160/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-141160/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-141160/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-141160/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-141160/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-141160/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141160" :question/id #uuid "91ad2ee8-eb6d-5323-a363-48d5ab23b581" :question/math-academy-id "q-141160" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨ia,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨ia,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true.  Indeed, the inner product in ${C}^{n}$ is linear in the first argument. So, a constant multiple from the first argument can be factored out.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument and linearity in the first argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}.$ Therefore, if $a\\ne 0,$ then\n\n$$\n⟨ia,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141160/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161/selection/e67c50ae6f057eb5b1613411032879e3a6424c11fde7b184a09c642292dad720" :answer/id #uuid "d5db2c9e-ec3c-5cd5-95a7-d523056e0a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7+4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161/selection/a0315038fcd50c30bb08415ad4bad05f4cdce1af32f0060d143e25f99cae9875" :answer/id #uuid "9bb4f2a1-62fb-51f0-a87d-b802ece00745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7-4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161/selection/db185e2ef33a51226400e16d8d431e35e632b4284eeee9c6e4f5f7a310847a2a" :answer/id #uuid "ac56175f-02af-5936-8661-96f49b5d8a21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7+8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161/selection/8bfed3389d809109073bb6c24d0ba899828cb65a9dee4584f0b46de669e973d6" :answer/id #uuid "21a46b06-586d-5437-aaf9-1bb3455accfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8+\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161/selection/297c7cf0644d34cb750744693e7ca0214303867bc1d72f5dcd505511a7b8cadf" :answer/id #uuid "0ffdcda1-c24e-51e4-943d-d5f7ff7f37a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8+7\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50a2b0a5-dc01-5c4b-be7f-8e93bb04a234" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141161/selection/db185e2ef33a51226400e16d8d431e35e632b4284eeee9c6e4f5f7a310847a2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-141161/selection/e67c50ae6f057eb5b1613411032879e3a6424c11fde7b184a09c642292dad720" "q-141161/selection/a0315038fcd50c30bb08415ad4bad05f4cdce1af32f0060d143e25f99cae9875" "q-141161/selection/db185e2ef33a51226400e16d8d431e35e632b4284eeee9c6e4f5f7a310847a2a" "q-141161/selection/8bfed3389d809109073bb6c24d0ba899828cb65a9dee4584f0b46de669e973d6" "q-141161/selection/297c7cf0644d34cb750744693e7ca0214303867bc1d72f5dcd505511a7b8cadf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141161" :question/id #uuid "d0f3a852-f21d-5ba1-9973-db675afd165e" :question/math-academy-id "q-141161" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=2-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=1+2\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩+⟨3b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2(\\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(2+\\text{i})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4+2\\text{i}+3+6\\text{i} \\\\  & =7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141161/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d59ac953-c511-5d6f-902d-4aeb804c99ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167/selection/b75a19026b1e374e012b476baf12a9e13b0376b2125b9d0594b169eecac197ba" :answer/id #uuid "75364442-42c3-561f-b9ac-c519065bafd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6+8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167/selection/dcb7c58c34d469d7c83ad6895d66b10f211dfac5b6db558d6ef705a3906bb905" :answer/id #uuid "3e95a633-20e9-5d84-8b07-c79f45acfa9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5+6\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167/selection/6072ffff3ae9885e76d3c148679958764492e8e99f4842b1cec2b3774fbc91d8" :answer/id #uuid "a4509992-50c1-5828-ab5b-07250578b3a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10+8\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167/selection/96f1a2091a9780aa09d677c4dbbf8ffb5f8ae927f16a7bcc84c13e2a20453513" :answer/id #uuid "31b5d283-2a55-541e-ae49-bd7e65c9d3e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12-3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167/selection/df74b35f9e4f978dfa740e6feb4abd3864b11ce85e9e10734ce3a5dd5b919ecf" :answer/id #uuid "76940e5b-58bc-5dbd-8b37-71eeea87b239" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "952730dc-add8-574d-835c-407db745d23a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97167/selection/96f1a2091a9780aa09d677c4dbbf8ffb5f8ae927f16a7bcc84c13e2a20453513" :answer-field/choices ["q-97167/selection/b75a19026b1e374e012b476baf12a9e13b0376b2125b9d0594b169eecac197ba" "q-97167/selection/dcb7c58c34d469d7c83ad6895d66b10f211dfac5b6db558d6ef705a3906bb905" "q-97167/selection/6072ffff3ae9885e76d3c148679958764492e8e99f4842b1cec2b3774fbc91d8" "q-97167/selection/96f1a2091a9780aa09d677c4dbbf8ffb5f8ae927f16a7bcc84c13e2a20453513" "q-97167/selection/df74b35f9e4f978dfa740e6feb4abd3864b11ce85e9e10734ce3a5dd5b919ecf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97167" :question/id #uuid "6140addf-ac61-581c-af38-58b12a2e258d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97167" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a-b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,c⟩=8+\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,b⟩=4-5\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a-b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ & =2⟨a,c⟩-\\overset{―}{⟨c,b}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨a,c⟩$ and $⟨c,b⟩:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩-\\overset{―}{⟨c,b}⟩ & =2(8+\\text{i})-(\\overset{―}{4-5\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =2(8+\\text{i})-(4+5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =16+2\\text{i}-4-5\\text{i} \\\\  & =12-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d59ac953-c511-5d6f-902d-4aeb804c99ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5545"] :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf y\\in\\mathbb C^3,$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle$ of the following two vectors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/assets/5d0567f732027d096d674c2513a41a9c32b87c78bb0203d60653d555c8c9a3b9.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
